t=0 keydown LEFT → schedule move(-1,0) at t=50 (if quiet)... but auto-repeat fires every 30ms and reschedules, with the last call always being move(-1,0). Release at t=500 → keyup → move(0,0) scheduled at 550 → at 550 velocity (0,0). Player never moved. Completely broken!

Phaser's keyboard plugin: by default... keydown's DOM auto-repeat is real. If I use trailing debounce with events, movement only fires after 50ms of no events. During hold, auto-repeat events keep coming → nothing happens. So pure trailing debounce makes movement unusable. Must use leading edge: `_.debounce(fn, ms, { leading: true, trailing: false })` → fires immediately on first event, swallows subsequent events until ms quiet. This gives responsive movement.

